      "side": 1,
      "message": "Could we add unit tests in `test/` comparing the `_c` and `_sse2` implementations of `av1_{lowbd,highbd}_generate_hog` and `av1_{lowbd,highbd}_compute_gradient_info_sb` across 8/10/12-bit inputs and edge cases (`dx \u003d\u003d 0`, `dy \u003d\u003d 0`, max gradients, odd/small dimensions, and padded strides)? None of these four new RTCD entry points currently have gtest coverage, and because SSE2 is always enabled on x86-64, the rewritten branchless C `get_hist_bin_idx` fallback is otherwise unexercised on x86-64 CI. (For `generate_hog`, `EXPECT_NEAR` with a small tolerance like `1e-6f` avoids 1-ULP x87 vs. SSE float rounding differences in `normalize_hog` on 32-bit x86 builds.)",
      "isAi": true,
      "revId": "f3889ab6ddfd370b4f171513b75040630117a39d",
      "serverId": "e5514cf8-2d6e-3e29-adb4-24cd6dde4bf0"
    },
