      "side": 1,
      "message": "+1 to guarding small widths: before this CL, `cols \u003c 3` never entered the inner loop and performed zero loads, whereas priming columns `0` and `1` now runs unconditionally whenever `rows \u003e\u003d 3`—doing wasted row loads when `cols \u003d\u003d 2` (reachable on 4:2:0/4:2:2 chroma right-edge blocks) and reading out-of-bounds at `row_*[1]` if a direct RTCD caller passes `rows \u003e\u003d 3 \u0026\u0026 cols \u003c 2`. Rather than returning early here in the `generate_hog()` wrapper (which wouldn\u0027t protect direct `av1_{lowbd,highbd}_generate_hog` callers and would skip `normalize_hog(total, hist)`), consider guarding the `r` loop with `if (cols \u003e\u003d 3)` inside `lowbd_generate_hog` (line 138), `highbd_generate_hog` (line 240), and their `_sse2` counterparts (`intra_mode_search_sse2.c` lines 64 and 164).",
